Fix these findings from the previous review:
```
error   Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CaddyWatchdog.cs:94 [correctness]: Watchdog quotes --config with doubled quotes, splitting paths that contain spaces — The script builds caddy's arguments as 'run --config ""' + $Caddyfile + '""'. Inside a PowerShell single-quoted string "" is two literal quote characters, not an escaped quote, so the command line becomes: run --config ""C:\path\Caddyfile"". Verified against CommandLineToArgvW: for a space-free path the doubled quotes cancel out and caddy receives [--config][C:\ELSE\Caddyfile] (works today), but for C:\Program Files\ELSE\ELSE.Caddy\Caddyfile it yields [--config][C:\Program][Files\ELSE\ELSE.Caddy\Caddyfile]. caddy then cannot find its config, exits non-zero, the watchdog exits, and WinSW spins on <onfailure> forever - the machine-wide proxy never comes up. KatalogCaddy.Sciezka() derives the folder from InstalledServiceHelper.TryGetDefaultBaseFolder(), and CaddyXmlWinSw.TrescXml plus CaddyInstallerTests (which asserts C:\Program Files\R&D\ELSE.Caddy\caddy.exe) treat spaced install paths as supported, so this is inconsistent with the module's own assumption. Should be '"' on each side. The existing test only asserts skrypt.ShouldContain("run --config"), so the quoting is uncovered.
```

