{"goalMet":true,"findings":[{"severity":"warning","category":"security","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/KatalogChroniony.cs","line":27,"title":"Protected directory keeps a foreign owner","detail":"Utworz() calls Directory.CreateDirectory then replaces the DACL, but never takes ownership. If the directory already exists, the existing owner keeps implicit READ_CONTROL/WRITE_DAC and can simply re-grant itself access after the Updater has locked it down. This is reachable on the KatalogCaddy fallback path (%ProgramData%\\ELSE\\ELSE.Caddy): the default ProgramData ACL lets a standard user create subfolders and become their CREATOR OWNER, so an unprivileged local user can pre-create the folder, wait for an install, then rewrite watchdog-caddy.ps1 - which CaddyInstaller.ZapiszDefinicjeUslugi writes there and WinSW runs as LocalSystem. The XML comment above the call names exactly this scenario as the thing it prevents. Setting the owner to Administrators/SYSTEM, or refusing to install into a pre-existing directory owned by someone else, would close it."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"robustness","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CaddyInstaller.cs","line":202,"title":"sc create stores an unquoted ImagePath","detail":"The argument string is `binPath= \"<path>\"`, so sc.exe consumes the quotes and writes ImagePath unquoted. CaddyXmlWinSw.TrescXml explicitly documents \"C:\\Program Files\\R&D\\ELSE\" as an ordinary base folder, so a path with spaces is expected here - and this is the classic unquoted-service-path shape for a service running as LocalSystem. BL_ServiceInstaller.cs:194 does the same thing, so this matches existing practice rather than regressing it; escaping the inner quotes (`binPath= \"\\\"<path>\\\"\"`) would make it consistent with the space handling the rest of the Caddy code already does."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"error-reporting","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CaddyfileWriter.cs","line":141,"title":"Same address in two apps' routes fails only at caddy validate","detail":"KluczGrupyBloku includes the route index, so two routes carrying the same host:port emit two site blocks with the same address and Caddy rejects the config. Deduplication exists inside one route (TrasaZUstawien.Adresy, MyEditorCertHosts.Dopisz, both with comments saying Caddy will not accept a duplicate host) but not across apps, and preflight cannot warn either: PortyPrzejmowane deliberately drops ports Caddy already listens on, so the second app sees no busy port. The save is safely rolled back, but the user gets raw `caddy validate` stderr instead of a message naming the app that already owns the address."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"organization","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CertificateProvider.cs","line":20,"title":"Many public types per file breaks the folder's own convention","detail":"CertificateProvider.cs is 604 lines holding ten public types (MaterialCertyfikatu, ICertificateProvider, IPokrycieCertyfikatu, four IPokrycieCertyfikatu implementations, AdresyZMagazynuWindows, DostawcaCertyfikatow, WindowsStoreCertificateProvider); ZajetoscPortow.cs holds four. Everything else in Logic/Caddy is one concept per file (AdminApiCaddy, KatalogKluczy, KatalogChroniony, AutomatyczneHttps), which is what makes the folder navigable, and finding PokrycieZapamietane currently means knowing it lives in a file named after a different type."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"ui-behaviour","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Controls/MyEditorHost.cs","line":67,"title":"Host and hint lists rebuild on every screen-state refresh","detail":"MyEditorHost.Typ and MyEditorHost.CzyCaddyDostepny call Przebuduj() unconditionally, and MyEditorCertHosts.PodpowiadaneAdresy calls PrzebudujPodpowiedzi() unconditionally. MyEditor.StanEkranuPropertyChangedCallback fires on every WybranyCertyfikat change, which for a text-mode CERTYFIKAT_HTTPS field is once per keystroke - so typing a thumbprint reassigns both Com