warning Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/KatalogChroniony.cs:27 [security]: Protected directory keeps a foreign owner — Utworz() calls Directory.CreateDirectory then replaces the DACL, but never takes ownership. If the directory already exists, the existing owner keeps implicit READ_CONTROL/WRITE_DAC and can simply re-grant itself access after the Updater has locked it down. This is reachable on the KatalogCaddy fallback path (%ProgramData%\ELSE\ELSE.Caddy): the default ProgramData ACL lets a standard user create subfolders and become their CREATOR OWNER, so an unprivileged local user can pre-create the folder, wait for an install, then rewrite watchdog-caddy.ps1 - which CaddyInstaller.ZapiszDefinicjeUslugi writes there and WinSW runs as LocalSystem. The XML comment above the call names exactly this scenario as the thing it prevents. Setting the owner to Administrators/SYSTEM, or refusing to install into a pre-existing directory owned by someone else, would close it.
```

