I ran the project's own build and test commands rather than reading the diff for verification.

**Build** — `MSBuild Else.Service.Updater.sln /p:Configuration=Debug`: succeeds. Only pre-existing warnings (the `.vdproj` installer project MSBuild can't build, and `netcoreapp3.1` EOL in `Haslo`). I also verified every new `.cs` file was hand-registered in the old-format `.csproj` files (per CLAUDE.md) — none is silently uncompiled.

**Tests** — `vstest.console.exe Else.Service.UpdaterTests\bin\Debug\Else.Service.UpdaterTests.dll`: **531 total, 530 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed** (30 s). The single skipped test is the `[Ignore]`d `Settings.txt`→`Settings.json` converter that CLAUDE.md documents as deliberately disabled — pre-existing, not caused by these changes. About 285 of those tests are new and cover the new Caddy logic.

**Goal.** The change set implements the non-invasive part of `PLAN-CADDY-ETAP1.md` §9: port-occupancy check with named culprit (1), process controller + preflight (2), `CaddyRoute`/`ICaddyfileWriter` (3), installer with pinned SHA-256 + WinSW + `sc failure` (4), watchdog + main-window status (5), `ICertificateProvider` (6), transactional write + reconcile (7), the inverted TLS qualifier rule + families + "binding unknown" warning (8), the `SERVICEHOST`/`WEBSITEHOST`/`CERTHOSTS` types and site hosting (9), and `OpenPorts` extended with the Caddy route port (10). Steps 11–14 (family A/B/C cutover) are deliberately deferred behind `BramkiWydaniowe.PrzejeciePortuUslugiGotowe`, which matches the plan's own dependency ordering — so services can't yet pick Caddy, websites can. The §1 rule ("Caddy never switches itself on") holds: with no app choosing Caddy, `KonfiguracjaCaddyAplikacji.Zastosuj` does one `File.Exists` and returns.

**Verified defect.** I confirmed the first finding by rendering a Caddyfile through the built assembly:

```
"http://https://serwer01" {
        request_body { max_size 99999999 }
        root * "C:/ELSE/www"
        file_server
}
```

`AdresBlokuSite.Blad("https://serwer01")` returns `null` and the preview reports `bez TLS - czysty HTTP`, so nothing stops the value before `caddy validate` rejects it — the raw-stderr outcome `AdresBlokuSite` was introduced to prevent.

```json
{"goalMet":true,"findings":[{"severity":"error","category":"correctness","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CaddyfileWriter.cs","line":203,"title":"Address with https:// prefix and no certificate gets a doubled scheme","detail":"ZJawnymBrakiemTls only tests StartsWith(\"http://\"), so \"https://serwer01\" fails the check and gets prefixed again, yielding the block address \"http://https://serwer01\". Verified by invoking CaddyfileWriter.Build on the built assembly with PublicHosts=[\"https://serwer01\"], Certificate=\"\". The value is not caught earlier: AdresBlokuSite.Blad(\"https://serwer01\") returns null (its regex allows an optional https?:// prefix), so TrasaZUstawien.OdmowNiepoprawnegoAdresu passes it and PodgladTrybowCertyfikatu shows \"bez TLS - czysty HTTP\". The save therefore reaches caddy validate, which rejects the quoted garbage token and rolls the transaction back with raw stderr - exactly the failure mode AdresBlokuSite exists to prevent. Also inconsistent with CaddyPreflight.PortyNasluchuTrasy/SondaTras, which read the address as an ordinary https URL. Either strip/reject the scheme in AdresBlokuSite, or make the prefix test scheme-aware (IndexOf(\"://\"))."},{"severity":"warning","category":"concurrency","file":"Else.Service.Updater/ViewModels/VMKonfiguracjaAplikacji.cs","line":773,"title":"Background Caddy reconciliation reads live, still-editable setting values","detail":"UzgodnijCaddy snapshots the list (Ustawienia.ToList()) but not the values, then hands it to MyThreadHelper.Execute. VKonfiguracjaAplikacji.xaml binds Value=\"{Binding CurrentValue, Mode=TwoWay, UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}\", so every keystroke mutates the same MySetting_AppSettingsItem instances the worker is reading. The reconciliation window is long by design (package download, sc create/start, GotowoscCaddy up to 60 s, validate, reload, SondaTras retries) and the config screen stays open and editable after the save reports success. A CERTHOSTS/SERVICEHOST/certificate edit made in that window can be picked up by the worker and written into routes.json + Caddyfile and reloaded into live Caddy, although the user never saved it - or fail the route build with a confusing error about an address the user was mid-way through typing. Snapshot (SettingType, CurrentValue) pairs before dispatching to the worker."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"resource-leak","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CertificateProvider.cs","line":329,"title":"RSA private key handle never disposed; key exported twice","detail":"MaterialDla calls Certyfikat.GetRSAPrivateKey(), which returns a new disposable RSA (CNG/CSP handle), and never disposes it. UzgodnienieCaddy.PrzygotujMaterialCertyfikatu calls Przygotuj once per address, so a route with several CERTHOSTS entries leaks one handle per address per save, released only at finalization. The same key is also exported twice - once in CzyEksportowalny(klucz) and again in PlikiTymczasoweZapisane via Klucz.ExportParameters(true) - so the probe could reuse the parameters it already obtained. Wrap the key in a using and pass the exported RSAParameters along."},{"severity":"suggestion","category":"robustness","file":"Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CertificateProvider.cs","line":413,"title":"SAN DER walk has no bounds checks and its failure escapes differently than other store failures","detail":"ZSan indexes San[pozycja], San[Pozycja + 1 + i] and Encoding.ASCII.GetString(San, start, dlugosc) without validating that the declared lengths stay inside the array, so a truncated or unusual SAN extension throws IndexOutOfRangeException/ArgumentOutOfRangeException. AdresyZMagazynuWindows.Adresy catches this and degrades to AdresyCertyfikatu.Nieznane (preview says \"internal certificate\"), but WindowsStoreCertificateProvider.MaterialDla calls Adresy(Certyfikat) unguarded, so the same certificate makes the save fail with a low-level exception while the preview promised a working route. Bound the walk to San