error   Else.Service.Updater/Logic/Caddy/CaddyfileWriter.cs:203 [correctness]: Address with https:// prefix and no certificate gets a doubled scheme — ZJawnymBrakiemTls only tests StartsWith("http://"), so "https://serwer01" fails the check and gets prefixed again, yielding the block address "http://https://serwer01". Verified by invoking CaddyfileWriter.Build on the built assembly with PublicHosts=["https://serwer01"], Certificate="". The value is not caught earlier: AdresBlokuSite.Blad("https://serwer01") returns null (its regex allows an optional https?:// prefix), so TrasaZUstawien.OdmowNiepoprawnegoAdresu passes it and PodgladTrybowCertyfikatu shows "bez TLS - czysty HTTP". The save therefore reaches caddy validate, which rejects the quoted garbage token and rolls the transaction back with raw stderr - exactly the failure mode AdresBlokuSite exists to prevent. Also inconsistent with CaddyPreflight.PortyNasluchuTrasy/SondaTras, which read the address as an ordinary https URL. Either strip/reject the scheme in AdresBlokuSite, or make the prefix test scheme-aware (IndexOf("://")).
